hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19586","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: Our land is a land of hunting; one of us shoots game and it disappears from him a night or two nights, then he finds it with his arrow in it. He said: If you find your arrow and find no trace of other than it in it, and you know that your arrow killed it, eat it."
"19587","Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from al-Shabi, Adi ibn Hatim informed us, he said: When this verse was revealed: Eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread, I took two cords, one black and the other white, and put them under my pillow. He said: Then I looked at them and could not distinguish the black from the white, nor the white from the black. In the morning I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what I did. He said: Your pillow is then wide indeed; that is only the whiteness of the day from the blackness of the night."
"19588","Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid and Zakariyya and others informed us, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with the mirad. He said: What strikes with its edge and pierces, eat, and what strikes with its side and kills, it is killed by a blow, so do not eat."
"19589","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I send the trained dog and it catches. He said: When you send your trained dog and mention the name of Allah and it catches, eat. I said: Even if it kills. He said: Even if it kills. He said: I said: I shoot with the mirad. He said: If it strikes with its edge, eat, and if it strikes with its side, do not eat."
"19590","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you but Allah will speak to him with no interpreter between Him and him. Then he looks to his right and sees only what he sent forth; then he looks to his left and sees only what he sent forth; then he looks before his face and the Fire confronts him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you can shield his face from the Fire even with half a date, let him do so."
"19591","Yahya narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Murayy ibn Qatari, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father used to uphold kinship, feed guests, and do such-and-such. He said: Your father sought something and attained it."
"19592","He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and find nothing to slaughter it with except flint and a stick. He said: Let blood flow with whatever you wish, then mention the name of Allah. I said: Food I avoid only from scrupulousness. He said: Whatever resembles Christian practice in it, leave it, so leave it."
"19593","Yahya narrated to us, from Mujalid, Amir informed me, Adi ibn Hatim narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me prayer and fasting. He said: Pray such-and-such, and fast; when the sun sets, eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread, and fast thirty days unless you see the crescent before that. I took two threads of black and white hair and looked at them and could not distinguish. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he laughed and said: O son of Hatim, that is only the whiteness of the day from the blackness of the night."
"19594","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Adi ibn Hatim said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I shoot game and seek its trace after a night, finding my arrow in it. He said: If you find your arrow in it and no beast has eaten from it, eat."
"19595","I mentioned it to Abu Bishr, and he said: from Said ibn Jubayr, from Adi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If you find your arrow in it and know that it killed it, eat."
"19596","Yahya narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Miqal, he said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard against the Fire even with half a date."
"19597","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Hudhayfah, he said: I used to narrate a hadith from Adi ibn Hatim, and I said: This Adi is in the region of Kufah; if I came to him I would be the one to hear it from him. I came to him and said: I used to narrate from you a hadith, and I wanted to be the one to hear it from you. He said: When Allah sent the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I fled from him until I was in the farthest land of the Muslims toward Byzantium. He said: I disliked my place where I was until I disliked it more than my dislike of the place I came from. He said: I said: I shall come to this man; by Allah, if he is truthful I shall hear from him, and if he is a liar he will not harm me. He said: I came to him, and the people looked at me and said: Adi ibn Hatim, Adi ibn Hatim, I think he said it three times. He said: He said to me: O Adi ibn Hatim, embrace Islam and be safe. He said: I said: I am a man of religion. He said: O Adi ibn Hatim, embrace Islam and be safe. He said: I said: I am a man of religion, he said it three times. He said: I know your religion better than you. He said: I said: You know my religion better than me. He said: Yes. He said: Do you not lead your people. He said: I said: Yes. He said: Muhammad mentioned al-Rakusiyyah, he said a word he sought to establish then left it. He said: It is not lawful in your religion to take the mirba. When he said it, I humbled a little. He said: And I see that what prevents you is poverty you see among those around me, and that people are united against us. Do you know the place of al-Hirah. He said: I said: I have heard of it but never came to it. He said: The riding woman will soon leave it without protection until she circuits - Yazid ibn Harun said: jawr, and Yunus from Hammad said: jawaz - then he returned to the hadith of Adi ibn Hatim - until she circuits the Kabah. The treasures of Khosrau ibn Hurmuz will soon be opened. He said: I said: Khosrau ibn Hurmuz. He said: Khosrau ibn Hurmuz. He said: I said: Khosrau ibn Hurmuz. He said: Khosrau ibn Hurmuz, three times. And soon one will seek someone to accept his wealth from him as charity and find none. He said: I have seen two: I saw the riding woman leave al-Hirah without protection until she circuits the Kabah, and I was among the cavalry that raided - and Yunus from Hammad said: raided al-Madain - and by Allah, the third will happen. It is the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he narrated it to me."
"19598","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal informed me, from al-Shabi, from Adi ibn Hatim, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If your shot falls into water, do not eat."
"19599","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Amr narrating from Adi ibn Hatim that a man came to him asking him about something he deemed small, then he swore. Then he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever swears an oath and sees another better than it, let him do the better and expiate his oath. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a hadith I never heard from anyone except my father."
"19600","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abbad ibn Hubaysh narrating from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The cavalry of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, or he said: The messengers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while I was at Aqrab, and they took my paternal aunt and some people. He said: When they were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: They were arrayed before him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the envoy is distant, the child is cut off, and I am an old woman with no service in me, so bestow favor upon me, may Allah bestow upon you. He said: Who is your envoy. She said: Adi ibn Hatim. He said: The one who fled from Allah and His Messenger. She said: So he bestowed favor upon me. She said: When he returned - and a man beside him, we think he is Ali - said: Ask him for mounts. He said: So she asked him, and he ordered for her. She said: She came to me and said: You did a deed your father would not do. She said: Go to him willing or unwilling; so-and-so came to him and got something, and so-and-so came to him and got something. He said: I came to him, and with him were a woman and children, or a child, and he mentioned their closeness to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I knew he is not a king of Khosrau nor Caesar. He said to him: O Adi ibn Hatim, what makes you flee from saying: There is no god but Allah - is there any god but Allah. What makes you flee from saying: Allah is Greatest - is anything greater than Allah. He said: I embraced Islam, and I saw his face brighten. And he said: Those who incurred anger are the Jews, and those astray are the Christians. Then they asked him, and he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, it is for you, O people, to give from surplus. Let a man give a sa, part of a sa, a handful, part of a handful. Shubah said, and most of my knowledge is that he said: A date, half a date. One of you will meet Allah and He will say what I say: Did I not make you hearing, seeing. Did I not give you wealth and children. What did you send forth. He looks before him, behind him, to his right, to his left, and finds nothing. He shields nothing from the Fire except with his face. So guard against the Fire even with half a date; if you do not find, with a gentle word. I do not fear poverty for you; Allah will help you and give you, or open for you, until the riding woman travels between al-Hirah and Yathrib, or more, fearing nothing for her mount but theft. Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shubah dictated it to me countless times, and I read it to him."
"19601","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay from Tamim ibn Tarafah from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: Two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then one of them pronounced the testimony and said: Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has attained right guidance, and whoever disobeys them both— whereupon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an evil speaker you are, stand up."
"19602","Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid informed us from al-Shabi from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with a dog, and he said: When you send your trained dog and mention the name of Allah over it, and it catches, and you reach it in time to perform the slaughter, then slaughter it, and if it kills it then eat, but if it eats from it then do not eat."
"19603","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Ayyub from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah from a man— Hammad said, and Hisham from Muhammad from Abu Ubaydah, and he did not mention: from a man— Hammad said, meaning: I used to ask people about the hadith of Adi ibn Hatim, and it was beside me and I did not ask about it, so I came to him and asked him, and he said: Yes, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent when he was sent, and I disliked him more intensely than I ever disliked anything at all."
"19604","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Muhammad from Abu Ubaydah from a man, he said: I said to Adi ibn Hatim: A hadith has reached me from you that I would like to hear from you, then he mentioned the hadith."
"19605","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Murayy ibn Qatari from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father used to uphold ties of kinship and used to do such and such, so is there for him in that any reward, meaning: He said: Your father sought a matter and attained it."
"19606","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from al-Amash from Khaythamah from Ibn Maqil from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves from the Fire. He said: Then he turned his face away until we thought he was looking at it, then he said: Guard yourselves from the Fire, and he turned his face away. He said: He said it two or three times: Guard yourselves from the Fire even with half a date, and if you do not find, then with a good word."
"19607","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal from Amir from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, we are people of hunting. He said: When one of you shoots with his arrow, let him mention the name of Allah Almighty, and if it kills then let him eat, and if it falls into water and he finds it dead then let him not eat it, for he does not know, perhaps the water killed it. And if he finds his arrow in game after a day or two and finds in it no trace other than his arrow, then if he wishes let him eat it. He said: And when he sends his dog against it, let him mention the name of Allah Mighty and Majestic, and if he reaches it having killed it then let him eat, and if it eats from it then let him not eat, for it only held for itself and did not hold for him. And if he sends his dog and it mingles with dogs over which the name of Allah was not mentioned, then let him not eat, for he does not know which of them killed it."
"19608","Hasan narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, that a man said: I said: I ask about the hadith of Adi ibn Hatim while I am in the region of Kufah, should I not be the one who hears it, so I came to him and said: Do you know me. He said: Yes. Then he mentioned the hadith, and he said in it: Are you not a Rakusi. I said: Yes. He said: Do you not lead your people. I said: Yes. He said: Do you not take the quarter-share. He said: I said: Yes. He said: That is not lawful for you in your religion. He said: My self became humbled, then he mentioned the hadith."
"19609","Yazid narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah and Asim al-Ahwal informed us from al-Shabi from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hunting with the mirad, and he said: What strikes with its edge then eat, and what strikes with its side then it is killed by a blow and dead. And I asked about hunting with a dog, and he said: When you send your dog and mention the name of Allah over it and it holds for you then eat, and if you find with it a dog other than your dog and it has killed it, and you fear it may have taken part with it, then do not eat, for you mentioned the name of Allah over your dog and did not mention it over the other."
"19610","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to us, and from people whom Shubah mentioned, from al-Shabi, he said: I heard Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the mirad, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it strikes with its edge then eat, and when it strikes with its side and kills then it is killed by a blow, so do not eat. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my dog. He said: When you send your dog and mention the name of Allah and it catches then eat, and if it eats from it then do not eat, for it only held for itself. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my dog and find with it another dog and I do not know which of them caught it. He said: Do not eat, for you only mentioned the name of Allah over your dog and did not mention it over the other."
"19611","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Ibrahim from Hammam from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you send your dog and mention the name of Allah, and it mingles with other dogs and they all take it, then do not eat, for you do not know which of them took it. And when you shoot and mention the name of Allah and it pierces then eat, and if it does not pierce then do not eat. And do not eat from the mirad except what you slaughter properly, and do not eat from the pellet except what you slaughter properly."
"19612","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Hammam ibn al-Harith from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I send my trained dog. He said: When you send your trained dog and mention the name of Allah and it holds for you then eat. He said: I said: Even if it kills. He said: Even if it kills, so long as no other dog shares with it. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, then I shoot with the mirad. He said: What pierces then eat, and what strikes with its side and kills then do not eat."
"19613","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Hammam from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, then he mentioned its meaning."
